+# CONTRACT — In-Memory Task Queue System
+
+The public API is the `TaskQueue` class exported from `src/index.ts`. It is a *manager*
+of multiple named queues (the "default" queue is used when no name is given). A logical
+clock (`options.now`) is injectable so delays/retries/schedules are deterministically testable.
+
+Comparator for selecting the next task among *available* tasks (documented decision):
+`(priority asc, availableAt asc, seq asc)` — priority dominates (Phase 3), availableAt breaks
+ties for delayed tasks (Phase 4), seq is the final FIFO tiebreak.
+
+## Phase 1 — Basic FIFO queue
+- [ ] `add(payload)` returns a task object with unique `id`, `status`, `createdAt` → test: two adds have distinct ids, status `pending`, numeric createdAt
+- [ ] new tasks start `pending` → test: `add().status === 'pending'`
+- [ ] `next()` returns oldest pending task and sets it `processing` → test: FIFO order + status transition
+- [ ] `next()` returns `null` when empty → test
+- [ ] `size()` reports waiting count → test: grows on add, shrinks on next
+
+## Phase 2 — Named queues
+- [ ] `add(p, {queue})` targets a named queue; omitting uses default → test: independence
+- [ ] `next(name)` pulls only from that queue → test
+- [ ] queues created implicitly on first add → test
+- [ ] `listQueues()` lists existing queue names → test
+- [ ] `next()` on non-existent/empty queue → `null` → test
+- [ ] backward compatible with Phase 1 → test (no-name add+next works)
+
+## Phase 3 — Priority
+- [ ] priority 1 (high) .. 10 (low), default 5 → test default + ordering
+- [ ] higher priority (lower number) returned first → test
+- [ ] same priority → FIFO → test
+- [ ] invalid priority (<1 or >10 or non-int) throws → test
+- [ ] priority is per-queue → test
+- [ ] task exposes `priority` → test
+
+## Phase 4 — Delayed/scheduled
+- [ ] `{delay}` ms or `{runAt}` absolute defers availability → test: not returned before time, returned after
+- [ ] non-delayed preferred over not-yet-available delayed → test
+- [ ] simultaneously-available delayed tasks ordered by availableAt, then priority, then FIFO → test
+- [ ] task exposes `availableAt` → test
+- [ ] delays work with named queues → test
+
+## Phase 5 — Retry with backoff
+- [ ] `complete(id)` / `fail(id, err)` finalize a processing task → test
+- [ ] failed task with retries remaining re-enqueued with delay `baseDelay*2^(attempt-1)` → test exact availableAt
+- [ ] default maxRetries 3, configurable per task → test exhaustion after N
+- [ ] default baseDelay 1000, configurable → test
+- [ ] task tracks `attempts` → test increments
+- [ ] retried task keeps queue + priority → test
+- [ ] exhausted retries → terminal `failed` state → test
+
+## Phase 6 — Dead letter queue
+- [ ] exhausted task moved to DLQ of its queue → test
+- [ ] `getDeadLetter(queue)` lists dead tasks → test
+- [ ] dead tasks retain error + failure count → test
+- [ ] `retryDeadLetter(id)` moves back for fresh retries → test (attempts reset, re-queued)
+- [ ] `clearDeadLetter(queue)` empties DLQ → test
+- [ ] DLQ is per-queue → test
+
+## Phase 7 — Dependencies
+- [ ] `{dependencies:[ids]}` blocks task until prerequisites complete → test
+- [ ] blocked task not returned by next → test
+- [ ] completing a dep unblocks dependents → test
+- [ ] circular dependency rejected at creation → test (pure cycle-detection unit test)
+- [ ] depending on non-existent task throws → test
+- [ ] failed dependency keeps dependents blocked → test
+- [ ] `getDependencyStatus(id)` inspectable → test
+
+## Phase 8 — Concurrency control
+- [ ] `setConcurrency(queue, n)` limits simultaneous processing → test
+- [ ] limit reached → next returns null despite pending → test
+- [ ] complete/fail frees a slot → test
+- [ ] default unlimited → test
+- [ ] `getConcurrency` / `getActiveCount` → test
+- [ ] highest-priority task still chosen subject to limit → test
+
+## Phase 9 — Progress + cancellation
+- [ ] `reportProgress(id, pct, msg?)` (0-100, else throws) → test
+- [ ] `getProgress(id)` → test
+- [ ] `onProgress(id, fn)` notifies on change, returns unsubscribe → test
+- [ ] cancel pending → removed from queue, status cancelled → test
+- [ ] cancel processing → status cancelled, slot freed → test
+- [ ] cancelled tasks never retried → test (fail after cancel does not re-enqueue)
+
+## Phase 10 — Recurring tasks
+- [ ] `schedule(cron, queue, template)` supports `*/N * * * *`, `0 * * * *`, `0 0 * * *` → test parse + next-occurrence (pure unit)
+- [ ] invalid cron throws → test
+- [ ] create / remove / list schedules → test
+- [ ] `tick(now?)` enqueues due tasks → test
+- [ ] enqueued recurring tasks are normal tasks → test
+- [ ] removing a schedule stops future occurrences → test
+
+## Phase 11 — Middleware pipeline
+- [ ] `use(queue, mw)` registers per-queue middleware; `setHandler(queue, fn)` sets handler → test
+- [ ] `runNext(queue)` runs middleware in order then handler → test ordering
+- [ ] middleware not calling next() skips handler → test
+- [ ] middleware can modify task → test
+- [ ] middleware throwing → task failed (retry/DLQ) → test
+- [ ] each queue has independent stack → test
+
+## Phase 12 — Graceful shutdown
+- [ ] `shutdown({timeout})` stops accepting tasks; add() throws after → test
+- [ ] waits for processing tasks up to timeout → test (completed)
+- [ ] tasks past timeout force-cancelled → test
+- [ ] `onShutdown(cb)` callbacks run → test
+- [ ] summary: {completed, forceCancelled, durationMs} → test
+- [ ] idempotent: multiple calls return same result → test
+- [ ] no processing tasks → completes immediately → test
+
+## Global validation
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles clean
+- [ ] `npm run lint` no errors
+- [ ] `npm test` all green
